               "summary":  "FPS is in a steep downtrend. At $18.00 it is below all three EMAs, down 73% from its June high, and just above its $17.67 record low after a 14% drop on 2026-11-20 with no company headline behind it. The selling comes from the CFO exit, slipping margins, the private-equity share overhang and sector-wide worries about AI spending. Demand is not the problem: revenue grew 69% and guidance went up. Technical stance: bearish. Moat thesis: watch. The AI-lab and hyperscaler customer traction looks real, but evidence of lasting pricing power is still thin."
